---
title: One cancel, from curl to the database and back (P07 Step 7 diagram, as implemented)
---
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor Client as curl
  participant Api as api.cancel<br/>(Starlette endpoint)
  participant UoW as unit_of_work<br/>(main.py wiring)
  participant Svc as BookingService<br/>(Reservations)
  participant Store as SqlReservationStore<br/>(Reservations internal)
  participant DB as SQLite file / PostgreSQL

  Client->>Api: DELETE /reservations/R101
  Api->>UoW: in_unit_of_work(cancel R101), worker thread
  UoW->>DB: connect()
  UoW->>Svc: BookingService(rooms, store, sender)
  Svc->>Store: find("R101")
  Store->>DB: SELECT ... FROM reservations WHERE id = ?
  DB-->>Store: R101, Maya, R7, 2026-11-12, 2026-11-14, Confirmed
  Store-->>Svc: Reservation R101 (remembered with status Confirmed)
  Svc->>Svc: reservation.cancel() - in memory only
  Svc-->>UoW: True
  UoW->>Store: save_changes()
  Store->>DB: UPDATE reservations SET status = 'Cancelled' WHERE id = 'R101'
  Store->>DB: COMMIT
  UoW->>DB: close()
  Api-->>Client: 204 No Content
  Note over Client,DB: A second DELETE finds R101 Cancelled: cancel() answers False, nothing is written, 404 NotFound.
  Note over UoW,DB: If anything raises inside the with-block, the wiring rolls back instead of save_changes: the request leaves no row behind.
